Neon containers port (M1), part 3 of 7: session persistence.

Keeps a tab in its container across session restore and reopen closed tab,
as brave-core v1.100.58 (bd6d26d1) does: the container id is encoded into
the saved URL as "containers+<id>:<url>" (virtual URL and PageState) and
decoded on load. Replaces Brave chromium_src overrides with plain hunks.
Also makes ChromeSerializedNavigationDriver::Sanitize call the base class,
which Brave patches the same way.

